    "id": "UgyoL5XOLD907FbDee14AaABAg",
    "parent": "root",
    "text": "In my opinion, using Sonnet generally doesn’t make much sense for me when it comes to coding. Opus 5.5 Medium has an Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index of 51 and a cost per task of $1.34. Sonnet 5.5 xhigh has an index of 52 and a cost of approximately $2.74. It’s much more expensive for nearly the same level of intelligence per task. Sonnet 5.5 High has an index of 47 and a cost of $1.08 per task. I’d rather use Opus 5.5 Medium as my default and pay a little more for greater intelligence. Speed might be a factor, though. It makes more sense to use MiMo-V2.6-Pro, which offers significantly lower costs while delivering nearly the same performance as Sonnet 5.5 High.",
